# Merge policy for syncing upstream releases into this fork.
#
# This fork rewrote both READMEs into its own patch documentation (upstream's
# original docs are linked from the top, not duplicated), so upstream's README
# edits are intentionally not merged: declaring them as "ours" turns a conflict
# into an automatic resolution.
#
# package.json is deliberately NOT listed. It is also edited here (scoped
# package name), but `merge=ours` on it silently discards upstream's dependency
# changes: a test merge produced zero conflicts while the version and the
# @deepseek-ai peer range stayed at the old values, which would break loading on
# the next DSH core line. It must be merged by hand — it is the one file where
# upstream's changes matter and cannot be detected automatically.
#
# Requires `git config merge.ours.driver true` in each clone; the driver is a
# built-in git convention but its definition lives in .git/config and does not
# travel with the repository. Without it the attribute degrades to an ordinary
# conflict rather than doing anything wrong.
README.md merge=ours
README.en.md merge=ours
